@cubic-dev-ai I don't think this one is valid. Vitest always excludes test files from coverage, whatever `coverage.exclude` says. Its config resolution appends the project's `test.include` patterns (plus setup files and the config file) to `coverage.exclude`, under the comment "Add hard-coded default coverage exclusions. These cannot be overridden by user config" (`vitest@5.0.x`, `resolveConfig`). So setting `exclude` here adds to that list and doesn't replace it.

It shows in the output too. `packages/x-performance/coverage/coverage-summary.json` lists `lib/size.mjs` and no `lib/size.test.ts`, and `packages/react-ai-sdk`'s lists `src/index.ts` and `src/index.native.ts` and neither `src/index.test.tsx` nor `src/index.native.test.ts`, with nothing in `exclude` naming them.

Adding `src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}` would be a no-op, so I'd leave the line as it is. Agree?

