I'll move the scope down into this PR: each of those 19 workspaces gets a `vitest.config.ts` here that holds only its coverage scope, and #8600 then only adds `thresholds` to it. A suggestion block can't add a file, so this is the proposed file for this package:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    coverage: {
      include: ["src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"],
    },
  },
});
```

The other 18 have the same shape, with these scopes (identical to what #8600 holds today):

| Workspace | `include` | `exclude` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `packages/{agent-launcher,create-assistant-ui,next,react-data-stream,react-hook-form,react-o11y,safe-content-frame,store,vite,x-generative-compiler}` | `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | |
| `packages/metro` | `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | `src/__fixtures__/**` |
| `packages/react-langchain` | `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | `src/__tests__/**`, `src/tests/**` |
| `examples/bundle-website-agent` | `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | |
| `examples/with-chain-of-thought` | `app/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | |
| `examples/with-elevenlabs-scribe`, `examples/with-livekit` | `app/**/*.{ts,tsx}`, `lib/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | |
| `examples/with-langgraph` | `app/**/*.{ts,tsx}`, `components/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | |
| `examples/with-expo` | the globs its #8600 config lists | |

The scope stays in the config file rather than a `--coverage.include` flag, because `sh` brace-expands `{ts,tsx}` in a script.

